      <div type="clause" n="El. 12">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> El. 12</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 12" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="30" ed="#liebermann"/>Ðeah hwa gebycgge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.1"/> his dohtor on<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.2"/> þeowenne, ne sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.3"/> hio ealles swa ðeowu<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.4"/> swa oðru<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.5"/> mennenu:<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.star"/> nage he hie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.6"/> út on elðeodig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.7"/> folc to bebycgganne. Ac gif he hire ne recce, se ðe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.8"/> hie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.6"/> bohte, læte hie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.9"/> freo on elðeodig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.7"/> folc. Gif he<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.10"/> ðon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> alefe his suna<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.11"/> mid to hæmanne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.12"/>, do hiere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.star2"/><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.13"/> gyfta: locige þæt hio hæbbe hrægl<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.14"/>; ⁊ þæt weorð sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.15"/> hiere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.16"/> mægðhades, þæt is se weotuma<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.17"/>, agife<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.18"/> he hire þone.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.19"/> Gif he hire þara<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.20"/> nan ne do, þon<hi rend="italic">ne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.21"/></hi> sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.3"/> hio frioh.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.22"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 12" corresp="#wit-g-prol-only"><pb n="30" ed="#liebermann"/>Ðeah hwa gebicge his dohtor ón ðeowenne, ne sie he<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.1-3"/> ealles swa ðeowu swa oðre mennenu: nage he hí ut on ælðeodig folc to bebycganne. Ac gif he hyre ne recce, se ðe hie bohte, læte hie faran freo on ælðeodig folc. Gif he þonne alyfe his sunea<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.1-3"/> mid to hæmanne, dó hyre gifta: locie þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> heo habbe hrægl; ⁊ þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> weorð sie hyre mægðhades, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> is sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.1-3"/> wituma, agyfe he hyre ðone. Gif he hire þara nan ne do, ðonne sie heo freoh.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 12" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="31" ed="#liebermann"/>Ðeah hwa gebicge his dohter to þeowte, ne beo heo alles swa þeow swa oðer þeowwifman: nage he hy utt on ælþeodig folc to syllanne. Ac gif he hyre ne recce, se þe hy bohte, læte hy frige on ælþeodig folc. Gif he þonne alyfe hys sune mid to hæmenne, do hyre gifta ⁊ locie þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> heo hæbbe hrægl; ⁊ þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> sy wurð hire mægþhades, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> his se wítuma, agyfe hire þene. Gif he hyre þare nanne ne dó, þonne sy heo freoh.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="El. 12" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="31" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis uendiderit filiam suam in famulam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.1-2"/>, non egredietur sicut ancillę exire<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.2-2"/> consueuerunt. Si displicuerit oculis domini sui cui tradita fuerat, dimittet eam; populo autem alieno uendendi non habebit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.3-2"/> potestatem, si spreuerit eam. Sin autem filio suo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.4-2"/> desponderit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.5-2"/> eam, iuxta morem filiarum faciet illi. Quodsi ei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.6-2"/> alteram acceperit, prouidebit puellę nuptias et uestimenta et precium pudicitię non negabit. Si ista<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.7-2"/> tria non fecerit, egredietur gratis absque pecunia.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="MP 12" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="234" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Ðeah hwa gebycgge his dohtor on þeowenne, ne sie hio ealles swa ðeowu swa oðru mennenu: nage he hie ut on elðeodig folc to bebycgganne. Ac gif he hire ne recce, se ðe hie bohte, læte hie freo on elðeodig folc. Gif he ðonne alefe his suna mid to hæmanne, do hiere gyfta: locige þæt hio hæbbe hrægl; ⁊ þæt weorð sie hiere mægðhades, þæt is se weotuma, agife he hire þone. Gif he hire þara nan ne do, þonne sie hio frioh.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="31" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenngleich<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.1"/> jemand seine Tochter zur Sklavin<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.2"/> verkauft<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.3"/>, so sei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.4"/> sie nicht gänzlich so Sklavin wie andere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.5"/> Unfreie.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.de1.star"/> Er<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.6"/> habe nicht Gewalt, sie auswärts an fremdes Volk<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.7"/> zu verkaufen.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.8"/> Aber<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.9"/> wenn der, welcher sie gekauft hat, ihrer nicht achtet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.10"/>, lasse er sie frei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.11"/> zu fremdem Volke. Wenn er aber seinem Sohne erlaubt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.12"/>, ihr beizuwohnen, so besorge er ihr<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.de1.star2"/><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.13"/> die Hochzeit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.14"/> (und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.15"/>) sehe zu, dass sie Kleidung habe; und was der Preis ihrer Jungfernschaft ist, das heisst das<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.16"/> Wittum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.17"/>, das gebe er ihr.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.18"/> Wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.19"/> er ihr keines von diesen [Dingen] schafft, dann sei sie frei.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Even if someone sells his daughter as a slave, she is not to be entirely a slave like other unfree women. He is not to have power to sell her abroad to a foreign people. But if the one who bought her does not care for her, let him let her go free to a foreign people. If, however, he allows his son to lie with her, let him provide her with the wedding (and) see that she has clothing; and what the price of her maidenhood is, that is the dower, let him give her that. If he provides her with none of these [things], then let her be free.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="235" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Though someone should buy his [the Christian slave’s] daughter in servitude, let her not be entirely as much a slave as other maidservants: he has not the power to sell her to a strange people. But if he does not like her, whom he bought, he shall let her go free among a strange folk. However, if he allows his son to have her, let him [the son] give her [marriage-] gifts: let him look that she have clothing; and the worth of her maidenhood, that is the bride-price, let him give her that. If he does none of these things for her, then let her be free.</ab>
        <note type="passageSource">Exodus 21,7–11</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="31">Exodus 21.7; Exodus 21.8; Exodus 21.9; Exodus 21.10; Exodus 21.11</note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">[Exodus 21, 7] | [21, 8] | [21, 9] | [21, 10] | [21, 11]</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="253"><ref target="clause:Af_El-to-29">Af El 29</ref></note>
