        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">31</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">31</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">disp. <hi rend="italic">Dm;</hi> disperderit <hi rend="italic">R;</hi> desponsauerit <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">disp. Dm; disperderit R; desponsauerit T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">31</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ea <hi rend="italic">R T;</hi> alteram ei <hi rend="italic">Vulg.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ea R T; alteram ei Vulg.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.7-2" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">31</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">t. i. <hi rend="italic">Vulg.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">t. i. Vulg.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-12.lnote.oe.1-3" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">30</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ælfreds bewusste Änderungen wollen wieder das Kapitel zwar dem Verständnis der Agsa. annähern und es so eindringlicher als Beispiel hinstellen, beweisen aber nicht die Absicht der Einführung ins praktische Recht. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Verknechtung 5—5b</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Ælfred’s deliberate changes are again meant, it is true, to bring the chapter closer to the understanding of the Anglo-Saxons and so to present it more forcefully as an example, but they do not prove an intention of introducing it into practical law. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Verknechtung 5—5b</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Sklaverei’ H; statt des für diesen Sinn seltenen <hi rend="italic">on,</hi> aus <hi rend="italic">in</hi> der Vulg., setzt <hi rend="italic">to</hi> Ld</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘slavery’ H; in place of <hi rend="italic">on</hi>, rare in this sense, from the Vulg.’s <hi rend="italic">in</hi>, Ld puts <hi rend="italic">to</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">bebycge</hi> wollen mit Ld bessern Wilkins, Thorpe, Wülfing <hi rend="italic">Syntax</hi> I 195. Auch Cosijn <hi rend="italic">Altwests. Gramm.</hi> II 168 belegt (<hi rend="italic">ge</hi>)<hi rend="italic">bycgean</hi> nur für ‘kaufen’. <hi rend="italic">S.</hi> jedoch <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Handel 1; Ine 11 H. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. ceapian,</hi> ahd. <hi rend="italic">koufon</hi> ‘erhandeln’ und ‘verhandeln’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Wilkins, Thorpe, Wülfing <hi rend="italic">Syntax</hi> I 195 would emend to <hi rend="italic">bebycge</hi> with Ld. Cosijn <hi rend="italic">Altwests. Gramm.</hi> II 168 too attests (<hi rend="italic">ge</hi>)<hi rend="italic">bycgean</hi> only for ‘buy’. <hi rend="italic">See</hi>, however, <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Handel 1; Ine 11 H. <hi rend="italic">Cf. ceapian,</hi> OHG <hi rend="italic">koufon</hi> ‘acquire by trading’ and ‘sell by trading’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Innerhalb des Standes der Unfreien (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 2a) anerkennt Ælfred verschiedene Grade</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Within the class of the unfree (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 2a) Ælfred recognizes different grades</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">H modernisiert, ebenso 21¹³</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">H modernizes, likewise 21¹³</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Af_El-to-12.lnote.de1.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">31</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Statt der nächsten zwei Sätze liest So:</hi> [21, 8] Wenn sie jedoch nicht gefällt den Augen ihres Herrn, der sie gekauft hat, so lasse er sie <hi rend="bold">frei</hi> ziehen; aber er habe nicht Gewalt, sie <hi rend="bold">auswärts</hi> an fremdes Volk zu verkaufen, wenn er ihrer nicht achtet.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Instead of the next two sentences So reads:</hi> [21, 8] But if she does not please the eyes of her lord who bought her, let him allow her to go <hi rend="bold">free</hi>; but he shall not have power to sell her <hi rend="bold">abroad</hi> to a foreign people, if he does not care for her.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">So’s Zufügung bleibt der Vulgata näher. Ebenso Ælfric’s Exodus: <hi rend="italic">gif heo mislicað þam hlaforde, forlæte hig!</hi> Ælfred liess in monogamischer Tendenz eine Zeile fort, die es als Regel ansieht, dass der Herr die Magd in seinen Harem aufnehme; <hi rend="italic">s. u.</hi> Erkl. 13</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">So’s addition stays closer to the Vulgate. Likewise Ælfric’s Exodus: <hi rend="italic">gif heo mislicað þam hlaforde, forlæte hig!</hi> Ælfred, with a monogamous tendency, left out a line which regards it as the rule that the lord takes the maidservant into his harem; see below note 13</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.7" n="7" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> unfrei 12e. f</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> unfrei 12e. f</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.8" n="8" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">H modernisiert, ebenso 21¹³</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">H modernizes, likewise 21¹³</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.9" n="9" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Logischer wäre ‘Sondern’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘But rather’ would be more logical</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.10" n="10" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘sich nichts aus ihr macht’; nicht: ‘nicht für sie Sorge trug’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘cares nothing for her’; not ‘did not provide for her’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.11" n="11" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘ziehen’ verdeutlichen aus Vulg. G So. Dies Verb der Bewegung kann im Agsä. fehlen; nicht ‘unter fremdem Volke’: <hi rend="italic">on</hi> drückt hier Ziel aus. — Unmöglich meinte Ælfred, was hier steht. Bei Unterdrückung der Kebsehe scheint er seinen Urtext nicht deutlich geändert zu haben, so dass ein Rudiment davon doppelt (<hi rend="italic">s.</hi> Erkl. 7) in den Text geriet</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">G So, following the Vulg., make ‘go’ explicit. This verb of motion can be omitted in A.-S.; not ‘among a foreign people’: <hi rend="italic">on</hi> here expresses goal. — Ælfred cannot possibly have meant what stands here. In suppressing concubinage he seems not to have altered his original text clearly, so that a remnant of it got into the text twice (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> note 7)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.12" n="12" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ælfred vermeidet ‘verlobt’ (<hi rend="italic">beweddað</hi> Ælfric) der Vulgata, wohl weil zwischen Freiem und Sklavin eine Verlobung dem Agsä. Rechte widerstreitet. Im Falle des Konkubinats zwischen Bauersohn und Magd wünscht er für letztere Verheiratung oder Freilassung</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Ælfred avoids the Vulgate’s ‘betrothed’ (<hi rend="italic">beweddað</hi> Ælfric), probably because a betrothal between a free man and a slave-woman conflicts with A.-S. law. In the case of concubinage between a ceorl’s son and a maidservant he desires marriage or manumission for the latter</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Af_El-to-12.lnote.de1.star2" n="**" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">31</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">was Töchtern zukommt. [21, 10] Wenn er eine andere [Frau für ihn] nimmt, besorge er ihr <hi rend="italic">fügt So zu.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">what is due to daughters. [21, 10] If he takes another [wife for him], let him provide her <hi rend="italic">is added by So.</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.13" n="13" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. o.</hi> Erkl. 6</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. above</hi> note 6</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.14" n="14" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">gifta</hi> auch Ælfric; nicht ‘Aussteuer’, zu trennen von <hi rend="italic">giftan</hi> (gen. sg.) für <hi rend="italic">dotem</hi> Ælfric <hi rend="italic">Exod.</hi> 22, 17 [<hi rend="italic">gifta</hi> (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Wb</hi>) <hi rend="italic">don:</hi> Hochzeit(sfest) machen <hi rend="italic">Leechdoms</hi> ed. Cockayne III 208]; richtig Schmid 603 (gegen frühere Übersetzung): ‘übergebe sie als Frau’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">gifta</hi> also Ælfric; not ‘dowry’, to be distinguished from <hi rend="italic">giftan</hi> (gen. sg.) for <hi rend="italic">dotem</hi> Ælfric <hi rend="italic">Exod.</hi> 22, 17 [<hi rend="italic">gifta</hi> (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Wb</hi>) <hi rend="italic">don:</hi> to hold a wedding (feast) <hi rend="italic">Leechdoms</hi> ed. Cockayne III 208]; correctly Schmid 603 (against an earlier translation): ‘give her as wife’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.15" n="15" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Die Vulgata nimmt zwei Fälle an: dass der Heiratende des Käufers Sohn sei oder ein anderer sei; jenen wünscht Ælfred als den einzigen; denn darum lässt er die Verheiratung des Sohnes mit anderer Frau fort. — Der Vulgata gemäss führen H So ‘und’ ein. — Wie <hi rend="italic">gesceawie</hi> braucht Ine <hi rend="italic">locige</hi> nur zur Verstärkung des folg. Verbs</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The Vulgate assumes two cases: that the man who marries is the buyer’s son, or that he is someone else; Ælfred wishes the former to be the only one; for that reason he omits the marriage of the son to another woman. — In accordance with the Vulgate, H So introduce ‘and’. — Ine uses <hi rend="italic">locige</hi>, like <hi rend="italic">gesceawie</hi>, only to reinforce the following verb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.16" n="16" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ælfred setzt hier nom. hinter <hi rend="italic">þæt is;</hi> sonst gebraucht er es partikelhaft und bringt die Erklärung in den Casus des zu Erklärenden; Wülfing <hi rend="italic">Syntax</hi> I 377</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Ælfred here puts the nom. after <hi rend="italic">þæt is;</hi> elsewhere he uses it as a particle and puts the explanation in the case of the thing explained; Wülfing <hi rend="italic">Syntax</hi> I 377</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.17" n="17" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Wittum. Für <hi rend="italic">dos</hi> als vom Bräutigam der Braut gezahlt <hi rend="italic">vgl.: iuvenis sortiri dote puellam;</hi> Aldhelm</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Wittum. For <hi rend="italic">dos</hi> as paid by the bridegroom to the bride <hi rend="italic">cf.: iuvenis sortiri dote puellam;</hi> Aldhelm</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.18" n="18" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘dann’ falsch, wie Ld So, die aber nur <hi rend="italic">þone</hi> verlasen; für letzteres bietet H späte Form</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘then’ is wrong, as are Ld So, which however merely misread <hi rend="italic">þone</hi>; for the latter H offers a late form</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-12.lnote.de.19" n="19" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Freilassung 10</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Freilassung 10</seg></note>
      </div>
